<title>UK: Cadbury up after SBC Warburg recommendation.</title>
<headline>Cadbury up after SBC Warburg recommendation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cadbury Schweppes Plc rose on Thursday after positive comment from analysts at SBC Warburg, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 8p at 585 by 1009 GMT in modest volume of less than one million shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at Warburg said the stock was cheap compared with an international peer group, Cadbury management was committed to above-average earnings growth and the stock should be supported by demerger speculation.</p>
<p>They put a demerged value of over 750p on the stock.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
